<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>paper-trends</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="report.css">
</head>
<body>
<nav class="masthead"><div class="row"><a class="brand" href="index.html">paper-trends</a></div></nav>
<main class="page">
<header class="title">
  <div class="kicker">Publication trends for academic conferences</div>
  <h1>What a field talks about, year by year</h1>
  <div class="meta"><span>Every paper of a conference from OpenAlex, read as rising and fading phrases, topic shifts and who publishes.</span></div>
</header>
{% for group, items in nav %}
<section>
  <h2>{{ group }}</h2>
  <ul class="glance">
  {% for slug, short, name, n in items %}<li><a href="{{ slug }}.html"><em>{{ short }}</em> — {{ name }}</a> <span style="color: var(--faint); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px">{{ "{:,}".format(n) }} papers</span></li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{% endfor %}
<section>
  <h2>Your own conference</h2>
  <p class="lede">These pages are generated ahead of time. Any conference indexed by OpenAlex can get the same page in two commands; venues outside the groups above land in a “More” group.</p>
  <pre class="code">uv run python -m paper_trends fetch "Design Automation Conference" --doi-prefix 10.1109/dac --years 2016-2026 --name dac
uv run python -m paper_trends report data/dac.jsonl --years 2016-2025 --out site</pre>
  <p class="lede">For live exploration — pick a term, see the papers behind it, compare venues — run the interactive app: <span class="mono">uv run streamlit run app.py</span>. Source and instructions: <a href="https://github.com/Minjia-Hu/paper-trends">github.com/Minjia-Hu/paper-trends</a>.</p>
</section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
